# Anchored, and for the same reason as the block below: on a case-insensitive
# filesystem an unanchored `Library/` also matches `src/llm_router/library/`,
# which hid six more source files.
/Library/

# Internal planning docs
.internal/

# Development-only directories — not needed by end users.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH. Unanchored, `agents/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, so it silently swallowed src/llm_router/agents/ and
# src/llm_router/library/ — 11 source files that existed locally, were never
# committed, and broke CI with "No module named 'llm_router.agents'".
#
# `llm_router.agents.session` is in server._CRITICAL_MODULES, so a published
# build missing it would have failed its own startup check — the failure would
# have reached users as a server that refuses to boot.
#
# Nothing here is meant to exclude anything under src/.
/research/
/deprecation/
/agents/
/demo/

# Internal docs — dev/strategy, not user-facing

# Unused README SVGs (removed from README)

# Deployment artifacts
Dockerfile
Procfile

# Local MCP config. The PLUGIN's own .mcp.json is committed (negated
# below): the scanner looks for it at the repo root, and a manifest
# pointing into a dot-directory instead reads as an unsafe declared path.
.mcp.json
!/.mcp.json

# Claude Code session/project artifacts (machine-specific)
.claude/sessions/
.claude/projects/
.claude/settings.json
.claude/mcp.json
tests/hook_rendering/

# Docs are local working notes — never commit (except the CI-generated benchmark page
# and versioned release-evidence packs, which are permanent records, not working notes)
/docs/*
!/docs/BENCHMARKS.md
# Generated from env_registry.PUBLIC (P3.8-a); tests and README depend on it.
!/docs/configuration.md
!/docs/releases/
!/docs/releases/**
# Bug entries, one file each (BUGS-1): /docs/* would keep them out of every clone.
!/docs/bugs/
!/docs/bugs/**
# Public, user-facing docs. /docs/* is ignore-by-default because this
# tree also holds internal strategy notes, so anything meant to SHIP has
# to be un-ignored explicitly. A page that is written but never committed
# is the same failure that left the Codex plugin pointing at a .mcp.json
# no clone ever contained.
!/docs/ROUTERARENA.md
# F107: retention of quota_history.jsonl (referenced by changelog.d/F107.fixed.md).
!/docs/RETENTION.md
# P2.4 ext-a: the empty-chain table tests/test_p24_empty_chain_table.py parses.
!/docs/empty-chain-behaviour.md
# The POST /ground contract — shipped surface, so it has to be readable by
# someone who does not have this checkout.
!/docs/GROUNDING_API.md
# `llm-router prefer` user documentation (P2.13): shipped surface.
!/docs/prefer.md
# The per-change KPI ledger — a permanent record (one row per merged PR), same
# category as /docs/repo_goals/ below, not a working note.
!/docs/KPI-LEDGER.md
# Bug record (symptom, cause, fix, test): a permanent record like the KPI ledger.
!/docs/BUGS.md
!/docs/decisions/
!/docs/decisions/**
# Preregistrations (hash recorded before the first scored row): permanent records.
!/docs/prereg/
!/docs/prereg/**
# The opt-in per-call proxy: user-facing enablement page, and the spike that
# is its design record (the numbers docs/proxy.md relies on).
!/docs/proxy.md
# A.6: framework/door integration guide (links every examples/ dir; read by tests/test_a6_examples_wired.py).
!/docs/integration.md
!/docs/spikes/
/docs/spikes/*
!/docs/spikes/per-call-proxy-2026-09-28.md
!/docs/spikes/local-speed-2026-09-28.md
# The North Star, its audit and the fix plan that comes out of it. Same
# category as /docs/decisions/ above: a permanent record of what the repo
# is supposed to do and where it currently doesn't, not a working note.
!/docs/repo_goals/
!/docs/repo_goals/**
# Measurement evidence. Same category as /docs/releases/ above — a permanent
# record, not a working note. Every number this project publishes is supposed
# to carry the file it came from, and a file no clone contains cannot be that
# file. Un-ignored after 14.0.0's CI caught the CHANGELOG citing four
# measurement documents and a seed record citing a fifth, none of which had
# ever been committed: `git add -A` skips ignored paths in silence.
!/docs/measurements/
!/docs/measurements/**
# The research this branch implements, referenced by ADR 0002. Vendored so the
# ADR's link resolves inside the repository rather than pointing at a file in
# somebody's Downloads folder — which only works if it is actually here.
!/docs/RESEARCH_SEMANTIC_LAYER.md

# Measured findings that outlive the session that produced them: a cross-backend
# quality benchmark, the local-execution proposal, and the backlog/plan they
# feed. Un-ignored deliberately — a number nobody else can read is a number
# nobody can check. AUDIT_ROUTING_*.md stays ignored: it is the raw forensic
# trace and carries local paths, session ids and spend.
!/docs/BACKEND-QUALITY.md
!/docs/BACKLOG.md
!/docs/PLAN_SAVINGS_ATTRIBUTION.md
!/docs/PROPOSAL_LOCAL_EXECUTION.md
!/docs/PLAN_ROUTING_OBSERVABILITY.md
!/docs/MEASUREMENT.md
!/docs/PLAN_LOCAL_EXECUTION_ROADMAP.md

